Transition and Animation in Prototypes
======================================

In UI/UX prototyping, transitions and animations make interfaces feel interactive and realistic.

They are heavily used in:
=========================
mobile apps
websites
desktop software
dashboards
game UI
smart devices

Tools like Figma and Adobe XD support prototype animations.

1. Transition
=============
A transition is the movement between:

screens
states
pages
components

Example:
========
Clicking a button opens another screen
A menu slides in
A popup fades in

Common Transition Types
========================
Transition	                        Description
==========                          ===========
Instant	                            Immediate change
Dissolve/Fade	                      Smooth fade
Slide In	                          Screen moves
Push	                              New screen pushes old
Move In/Out	                        Object motion
Smart Animate	                      Automatic object animation

2. Animation
============
Animation adds:
===============
motion
timing
feedback
realism

Example:
========
Button bounce
Loading spinner
Hover effect
Expanding cards
Animated menu

Common UI Animations
====================
Animation	                        Purpose
Hover Animation	                  User feedback
Ripple Effect	                    Touch interaction
Loading Spinner	                  Waiting indicator
Bounce	                          Attention
Scale Animation	                  Emphasis
Parallax	                        Depth effect
Smooth Scroll	                    Natural movement

In Figma Prototyping
=====================

In Figma you can:
=================
connect frames
add interactions
choose transition styles
animate components

Typical Prototype Flow
======================
Frame A
   ↓ click
Transition
   ↓
Frame B
   ↓ hover
Animation


Smart Animate automatically animates:
=====================================
position
size
opacity
rotation
color

between two frames.

Example:
=========
Button expands into dialog
Card transforms into detail page
Sidebar smoothly opens

Difference Between Transition and Animation
===========================================
Transition	                              Animation
Moves between screens/states	            Animates objects/elements
Navigation focused	                      Motion focused
Usually larger changes	                  Usually smaller interactions
Screen-level	                            Component-level

Prototype Animation Workflow
============================
Wireframe
   ↓
UI Design
   ↓
Prototype Connections
   ↓
Transitions
   ↓
Animations
   ↓
Interactive Prototype

Common UX Animation Principles
==============================
Good animations should be:

fast
smooth
meaningful
non-distracting

Popular timing:
===============
150ms–400ms

Common Tools
============
Tool                  	  Animation Support
====                      =================
Figma	                    Excellent
Adobe XD	                Good
Framer	                  Advanced
ProtoPie	                Very Advanced
Principle	                Advanced
After Effects	            Motion Graphics

UX/UI Terms Related to Animation
================================
Motion Design
Microinteractions
Interaction Design
State Changes
Easing
Keyframes
Gesture Animation
Interactive Prototype
Dynamic UI
Responsive Motion

Which option do we use in Figma for transition and animation?
=============================================================
In Figma, transitions and animations are mainly created in the Prototype tab.

Main Option Used: Prototype Tab

Steps:

Select a frame or object
Open the right sidebar
Click Prototype
Connect one frame to another
Choose:
    interaction      
    transition
    animation

Important Options Inside Prototype
==================================
Option	                  Purpose
======                    =======
Navigate                  To	Move to another frame
Open Overlay	            Popup/modal
Change To	                Switch component states
Smart Animate	            Automatic animation
Instant	                  No animation
Dissolve	                Fade transition
Slide In/Out	            Sliding motion
Push	                    Push transition
Move In/Out	              Object movement

Most Popular Animation Option
=============================
Smart Animate

This is the most commonly used animation feature in Figma.

It automatically animates:

movement
resizing
opacity
rotation
color changes

between two frames.

Where It Appears
================
Example:

Prototype
   └── Interaction
          ├── On Click
          ├── Navigate To
          └── Animation
                 ├── Instant
                 ├── Dissolve
                 ├── Smart Animate
                 ├── Move In
                 └── Slide In

Common Triggers
================
Trigger	                    Meaning
=======                     =======
On Click	                  Mouse click
On Drag	                    Drag interaction
While Hovering	            Hover effect
Mouse Enter	                Cursor enters
Mouse Leave	                Cursor exits
After Delay	                Auto animation

Common Animation Settings
=========================
Setting	                    Purpose
Ease In	                    Starts slow
Ease Out	                  Ends slow
Ease In and Out	            Smooth motion
Linear	                    Constant speed
Duration	                  Animation speed
Component                   Animation

For buttons, toggles, menus:
============================
Use:

Components
Variants
Change To
Smart Animate

Example:
========
Button Default
   ↓ hover
Button Hover
   ↓ click
Button Pressed

Best Figma Features for Animation
=================================
Feature	                      Use
=======                       ===
Smart Animate	                General animation
Interactive Components	      Button states
Overlays	                    Popups/modals
Variants	                    UI state changes
Auto Layout	                  Smooth resizing
Prototype Connections	        Navigation flow

Professional Workflow
====================
Design Frame
   ↓
Create Variants
   ↓
Prototype Connections
   ↓
Smart Animate
   ↓
Preview Prototype



